// Title: Hacktool Execution - PE Metadata
// Sigma ID: 37c1333a-a0db-48be-b64b-7393b2386e3b
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-04-27 | Modified: 2024-01-15
// ATT&CK: credential-access, resource-development, T1588.002, T1003
// Description: Detects the execution of different Windows based hacktools via PE metadata (company, product,
//   etc.) even if the files have been renamed
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://github.com/cube0x0
//   - https://www.virustotal.com/gui/search/metadata%253ACube0x0/files
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_hktl_execution_via_pe_metadata.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessVersionInfoCompanyName =~ "Cube0x0"
